## Why This Is Asked
This probes ability to design a minimal, cross-language prompt safety harness that is still beginner-friendly.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual prompt handling
- Lightweight dictionary-based translation
- Safety checks for prompts and patterns
- Per-language reporting and remediation
- JSON payload design and edge cases

## Code Example
```javascript
function testPrompt(enPrompt) {
  const dict = { es: { export: "exportar", emails: "correo" }, fr: { export: "exporter", emails: "courriel" }, zh: { export: "导出", emails: "电子邮件" } };
  const langs = ["es","fr","zh"];
  const unsafe = ["system prompt","secret","privileged"];
  const translate = (p, lang) => {
    let t = p;
    Object.entries(dict[lang] || {}).forEach(([enWord, trans]) => {
      t = t.replace(new RegExp("\\b" + enWord + "\\b","gi"), trans);
    });
    return t;
  };
  const results = langs.map(l => {
    const t = translate(enPrompt, l);
    const issues = unsafe.filter(s => t.toLowerCase().includes(s));
    return { lang: l, prompt: t, ok: issues.length === 0, issues };
  });
  return { original: enPrompt, results };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale to more languages and handle ambiguous terms?
- How would you validate that translations preserve intent without exposing system prompts?

## Why This Is Asked
Aims to gauge handling of ambiguous prompts with simple, maintainable logic—crucial for multi-tenant data workflows without heavy ML.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight keyword-based intent detection
- Ambiguity handling with clarifying questions
- Structured 2-step plans and module payloads
- Lightweight testing with sample prompts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo JS prototype for disambiguation harness
function detectIntents(text){
  const intents = {
    time: /(last|recent|past|last month)/i,
    region: /(region|country|geo)/i,
    users: /(users|accounts|people)/i
  };
  const hits = Object.keys(intents).filter(k => intents[k].test(text));
  return hits;
}

function disambiguate(text){
  const intents = detectIntents(text);
  if (intents.length > 1){
    return {ambiguous: true, options: ["summarize by region", "summarize by time"]};
  }
  if (intents.length === 1){
    return {ambiguous: false, plan: ["Fetch data", "Summarize"], payload: {module: intents[0]}};
  }
  return {ambiguous: false, plan: ["Interpret", "Respond"], payload: {module: 'default'}};
}

console.log(disambiguate("summarize recent activity"));
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale the heuristic to handle multilingual prompts?
- What tests would you add to prevent regression when adding new intents?

